<p>Because Formspree and Google are based overseas, your information may be stored or processed outside New Zealand. We only use providers that offer protections comparable to those required by the Privacy Act.</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>This website sets a small number of <strong>analytics cookies</strong> through Google Analytics — <code>_ga</code> and one starting <code>_ga_</code>. They let us tell a returning visitor from a new one and see which pages lead to enquiries. They expire after two years, and you can clear or block them in your browser at any time without breaking anything on this site.</p>
<p>That is the extent of it. Specifically, this website does <strong>not</strong>:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Run advertising cookies or cross-site advertising pixels</li>
  <li>Use Google Signals, which is the setting that would link your activity here to your wider Google advertising profile — we have it switched off</li>
  <li>Sell or share the data with anyone for advertising</li>
</ul>
<p>New Zealand has no cookie-banner law equivalent to the EU's, and we would rather explain what we set than make you dismiss a pop-up to read the page. If you would prefer not to be counted at all, Google publishes a browser <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">opt-out add-on</a>, or your browser's private mode will do the same job.</p>

<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>If you become a client:</strong> we keep your contact details for as long as we're working together, and afterwards for as long as we're legally required to keep business records (currently seven years under New Zealand tax law).</li>
  <li><strong>If you enquire but don't proceed:</strong> we keep your enquiry for up to 24 months in case you come back, then delete it.</li>
  <li><strong>If you ask us to delete it:</strong> we delete it, other than anything we're legally obliged to retain.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How we protect it</h2>
<p>The site is served over HTTPS with a valid SSL certificate. Form submissions are encrypted in transit. Access to enquiry data is limited to the people at WFT who need it to contact you.</p>
<p>No system is perfectly secure, and we won't pretend otherwise. If a privacy breach occurs that is likely to cause you serious harm, we will notify you and the Office of the Privacy Commissioner as required by the Privacy Act 2020.</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>Under the Privacy Act 2020 you have the right to:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Ask what we hold about you</strong> — we'll tell you, free of charge.</li>
  <li><strong>Correct anything that's wrong</strong> — we'll fix it.</li>
  <li><strong>Ask us to delete it</strong> — we'll do that too, subject to our record-keeping obligations.</li>
</ul>
<p>Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and we'll respond within 20 working days, which is the statutory timeframe.</p>

<h2>Complaints</h2>
<p>If you think we've mishandled your personal information, tell us first — we'd rather fix it directly. If you're not satisfied with our response, you can complain to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner at <a href="https://www.privacy.org.nz" rel="noopener">privacy.org.nz</a> or 0800 803 909.</p>

<h2>Websites we build for clients</h2>
<p>This policy covers <strong>this</strong> website only. If we build a website for your business, that site is yours and you are the one responsible for its privacy policy and for any personal information your customers give you through it. We'll help you get a sensible policy in place as part of the build, but the legal responsibility sits with you as the site owner.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If we change how we handle personal information, we'll update this page and change the "last updated" date at the top. Material changes will be obvious, not buried.</p>

